Ques5: Explain how a drone performs take-off, landing, hovering, move forward, move backward, move left, move right, and rotate (yaw) ?
Take - off:
→ All four motors spin faster.
→ The drone goes upward.
Landing:
→ All motors slow down.
→ The drone comes down safely.
Hovering:
→ All four motors spin at the same speed.
→ The drone stays at one place in the air.
Move Forward:
→ Back motors spin faster than front motors.
→ The drone moves forward.
Move Backward:
→ Front motors spin faster than back motors.
→ The drone moves backward.
Move Left:
→ Right-side motors spin faster.
→ The drone moves left.
Move Right:
→ Left-side motors spin faster.
→ The drone moves right.
Rotate (Yaw):
→ CW and CCW motors change their speed.
→ The drone rotates left or right without changing its position.
